  <body>
    <div id="img-container">
      <a href="http://www.example.com"><img src="image.jpg" alt="Image"></a>
      <p>Caption goes here</p>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
```

In this example, we have an `<img>` tag with a `src` attribute set to the path of the image file and an `alt` attribute set to a descriptive alternative text for the image. We also have a `<p>` tag with some text that will serve as the caption for the image. The `<div>` tag with the `id` attribute set to "img-container" is used to style and position the image and caption together.

The `<a>` tag with the `href` attribute set to the URL of the web page you want to link to is used to make the image a hyperlink. When a user clicks on the image, they will be redirected to the specified URL.

The CSS styles are applied to the `#img-container` div to center the image and caption horizontally, and to set the maximum width of the image to 100% and the height to auto to ensure that the image maintains its aspect ratio. The `font-style` property is set to italic to style the caption text.

