* The right to receive a product that is free from defects and faults.
* The right to receive a product that is safe to use and does not pose any risk to the consumer.
* The right to receive a product that is delivered on time and in accordance with the agreed-upon delivery schedule.
* The right to receive a product that is priced fairly and reasonably.
* The right to receive a product that is backed by a clear and concise warranty or guarantee.
* The right to receive a product that is easy to return or exchange if it does not meet the consumer's expectations.

These consumer rights are designed to protect consumers from unfair practices and ensure that they receive the products and services they expect and deserve.

