response:
To implement the bubble sort algorithm in C++ for the given JSON data, follow these steps:

1. Include necessary headers:
```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <algorithm>
```
1. Define a function to perform bubble sort on a vector of integers:
```cpp
void bubbleSort(std::vector<int>& arr) {
    int n = arr.size();
    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
            if (arr[j] > arr[j + 1]) {
                std::swap(arr[j], arr[j + 1]);
            }
        }
    }
}
```
1. Read the JSON data and convert it to a vector of integers:
```cpp
std::string jsonData = R"({
  "array": [5, 2, 9, 1, 5, 6]
})";

nlohmann::json json = nlohmann::json::parse(jsonData);
std::vector<int> arr = json["array"].get<std::vector<int>>();
```
1. Sort the vector using the bubbleSort function:
```cpp
bubbleSort(arr);
```
1. Print the sorted vector:
```cpp
for (auto num : arr) {
    std::cout << num << " ";
