```javascript
function searchPlace() {
  var sheet = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSheet();
  var dataRange = sheet.getRange("A1:D"); // Assuming your data is in columns A to D
  var values = dataRange.getValues();

  for (var i = 1; i < values.length; i++) {
    var placeName = values[i][0];
    var apiKey = "YOUR_API_KEY"; // Replace with your Google Maps API key
    var url = `https://maps.googleapis.com/maps/api/geocode/json?address=${placeName}&key=${apiKey}`;

    var response = UrlFetchApp.fetch(url);
    var json = JSON.parse(response);

    if (json.results.length > 0) {
      var latitude = json.results[0].geometry.location.lat;
      var longitude = json.results[0].geometry.location.lng;

      values[i][1] = latitude;
      values[i][2] = longitude;
    } else {
      values[i][1] = "";
      values[i][2] = "";
    }
  }

  sheet.getRange("A1:D").setValues(values);
}
```

Replace `YOUR_API_KEY` with your actual Google Maps API key. This script will search for each place name in the specified column and store the latitude and longitude in the next two columns.

